---
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site.js';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="Important limits on the technical, capacity, performance and project information published on the Haiyun Grain Machine website."
  lede="This page explains what the technical content on this site can and cannot be used for. It is a website disclaimer, not a substitute for a signed contract or site-specific engineering review."
>
  <h2>1. General information</h2>
  <p>
    The content on {site.url} is published for general business and technical evaluation. It
    describes standard equipment, typical configurations and general milling practice. It is not
    a substitute for a site survey, a wheat analysis, a structural assessment, an electrical design
    or a qualified engineer's review of your project.
  </p>

  <h2>2. No professional advice</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing on this site constitutes engineering, legal, tax, safety, environmental or financial
    advice. You should obtain advice from qualified professionals in your jurisdiction before
    committing capital, ordering equipment, constructing a building or changing a process.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Capacity and performance</h2>
  <p>
    Capacity figures are nominal and depend on the basis stated for the table or model. Actual
    output varies with wheat variety, moisture, bulk density, extraction rate, product mix, roll
    condition, ambient conditions, operating hours, power quality and operator skill. A capacity
    shown as t/d may refer to wheat intake or finished flour; the quotation and flow sheet state
    the contractual basis.
  </p>
  <p>
    Power, ash, extraction, staffing and consumption figures are indicative. They are not a
    guarantee of performance at your site. Performance tests, acceptance criteria and remedies are
    defined in the signed contract, not on this website.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Technical information may change</h2>
  <p>
    We review and update content, but equipment, standards and recommended practice change. A page
    may not reflect the latest model, option, regulation or safety requirement. The date on an
    article is not a guarantee that every statement remains current. Confirm the current
    specification with our technical team before ordering.
  </p>

  <h2>5. No offer or contract</h2>
  <p>
    Product descriptions, photographs, dimensions, prices, lead times and project examples are
    invitations to enquire. They are not an offer capable of acceptance and do not create a
    contract. A binding obligation arises only from a written quotation or contract signed by
    authorised representatives of both parties.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Project examples</h2>
  <p>
    Reference projects describe configurations and results achieved in specific conditions. They
    are not a promise that a similar plant will achieve the same output, extraction, energy use or
    payback at another site. Wheat, climate, building, power, labour and management differ.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Third-party information and links</h2>
  <p>
    We may refer to standards, regulations, suppliers or external websites. We do not control those
    sources and are not responsible for their accuracy, availability or security. A link is not an
    endorsement of every statement on the destination page.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Safety and compliance</h2>
  <p>
    Milling equipment involves rotating machinery, dust, heat, electrical systems and confined
    spaces. Installation and operation must follow the approved drawings, local electrical and
    safety rules, lockout/tagout procedures and the operator manual. This website does not replace
    those documents or the training provided at commissioning.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Export and end-use</h2>
  <p>
    Export, re-export and end-use may be subject to sanctions, export-control and customs rules.
    Customers are responsible for providing accurate end-use, end-user and destination information.
    See the <a href="/export-compliance/">Export Compliance</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, we exclude liability for indirect, incidental or consequential
    loss arising from reliance on this website. Nothing in this disclaimer limits liability for
    death or personal injury caused by negligence, fraud, or any liability that cannot lawfully be
    excluded. Mandatory rights under applicable law are not affected.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    To confirm a specification or discuss a project, contact {site.legalName} at
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or {site.phone}.
    See also the <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a> and
    <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
